// ~~ Tooltips {
var string tt1="Number of historical bars used by the large rolling volume profile. The same lookback is reconstructed historically when a pivot is evaluated, so old pivots are judged only with information available at that time."
var string tt2="Number of price rows used to discretize the rolling profile. More rows increase price resolution but also increase drawing and calculation load."
var string tt3="Maximum horizontal width of the displayed profile in chart bars. The POC row reaches this width; other rows scale relative to it."
var string tt4="Horizontal gap between the current bar and the left edge of the displayed rolling profile."
var string tt5="Master switch for the large rolling profile shown at the right side of the chart."
var string tt6="Highlight the highest-volume profile row and draw its short guide line and price label."
var string tt7="Outline profile rows that currently contain an active profile-guided support or resistance level."
var string tt8="Left/right pivot confirmation length. A value of 5 means a pivot is confirmed five bars after the actual swing bar."
var string tt9="Maximum ATR distance around a raw pivot in which the profile engine may search for a stronger nearby volume node."
var string tt10="Minimum candidate-node volume relative to the profile POC. Lower values admit weaker nearby profile structure."
var string tt11="Minimum combined profile evidence needed before a raw price pivot can become an active level."
var string tt12="Maximum fraction of the distance from the raw pivot toward the selected profile node. Actual pull is scaled by profile evidence."
var string tt13="Minimum final 0-100 score required after profile evidence, absorption, relative pivot volume and wick rejection are combined."
var string tt14="Maximum number of active profile-guided levels. When exceeded, the weakest active level is removed first."
var string tt15="Same-side levels within this ATR distance are treated as duplicates. A stronger new candidate replaces the weaker nearby level."
var string tt16="ATR buffer beyond an active level required for a confirmed close to invalidate that level."
var string tt17="Color used for active support levels, support endpoint dots and support profile-row outlines."
var string tt18="Color used for active resistance levels, resistance endpoint dots and resistance profile-row outlines."
var string tt19="Accent color used for the inner profile-confirmed pivot core and the raw-pivot-to-final-level pull guide."
var string tt20="Color of the faint raw price pivot marker before the profile engine relocates the final level."
var string tt21="Estimated buying-volume color in the large profile. Buy/sell attribution comes from candle close location inside each bar range."
var string tt22="Estimated selling-volume color in the large profile. Buy/sell attribution is approximate rather than true bid/ask volume."
var string tt23="Color used for the displayed profile point of control."
var string tt24="Shared line style used by active support and resistance levels."
var string tt25="Show the layered profile-confirmed pivot marker at the final relocated level price."
var string tt26="Show the faint raw pivot marker and dotted vertical guide connecting it to the final profile-guided level."
var string tt27="Show the final 0-100 level score inside the historical profile-confirmed pivot marker."
var string tt28="Show the current endpoint dot and one-number score label at the right edge of each active level."
var string tt29="Score added to an active level each time a new same-side pivot lands within the merge distance without beating its score. Retests reinforce the level instead of being discarded. 0 disables."
var string tt30="Remove active levels older than this many bars since their pivot. 0 keeps levels until they break or are trimmed."
var string tt31="Value Area: the price band around the POC holding this share of the profile volume. VAH/VAL are drawn on the profile and used as location confluence. Context Refresh: bars between recalculations of the POC/VA used by the signal engine (lower = more precise, heavier)."
var string tt32="Intrabar: buy/sell share comes from the volume-weighted close location of each lower-timeframe candle inside the chart bar (much finer than the chart bar alone). Bar Estimate: close location of the chart bar only. Falls back to Bar Estimate automatically when intrabar data is missing or the Intrabar TF is not lower than the chart."
var string tt33="Lower timeframe for Intrabar delta. On 2-3m MNQ/MES use 1 (any plan) or 30S/15S/10S if your TradingView plan includes seconds data. Delta Avg Len: bars averaged for the delta-flip threshold."
var string tt34="Signals fire on confirmed bars only. Each candidate gets confluence points and a grade. Only grades at or above Min Grade are shown, alerted and counted in the stats."
var string tt35="Points needed for each grade. Max is about 11.5: level score (0-3), HTF trend (+2/+1/-2), VWAP side (+1), value-area location (+1), extra triggers (+1 each, max +2), bar delta in favor (+1), relative volume >= 1.2x (+1), level touched by 2+ pivots (+0.5)."
var string tt36="Only levels with at least this score can produce signals. Touch Zone: ATR distance beyond the level that still counts as a test of it within the last 3 bars."
var string tt37="Triggers (at least one required, with a confirmation close in the trade direction): Sweep & Reclaim = a wick runs the level and the bar closes back on the right side. Absorption = high-volume small-body bar at the level. Delta Flip = delta turns strongly in favor after opposite delta. Break & Retest = first test of a broken level from the other side."
var string tt38="Flip Broken Levels: a broken level is kept once with the opposite role (old resistance becomes support) for Break & Retest setups. Cooldown: minimum bars between signals."
var string tt39="Higher-timeframe trend from EMA 50/200 on the HTF, using the last closed HTF bar (no repaint). Hard: longs only in HTF uptrend, shorts only in downtrend. Score: counter-trend allowed but penalized. Off: ignored."
var string tt40="Signals only inside this session (exchange time zone below). Default skips the first and last minutes of the NY cash session where MNQ/MES spreads and whipsaws are worst. Close at Session End: open trades are closed at the first bar outside the session."
var string tt41="ATR(14) percentile over the last 500 bars. Signals are blocked when volatility is unusually low (chop) or extreme (news spikes)."
var string tt42="Minimum distance, in R, from entry to the nearest opposite level. Avoids trades that run straight into the next wall before reaching target."
var string tt43="Stop goes beyond the tested level and the touch extreme by this ATR buffer. Signals whose stop is wider than Max Risk ATR are skipped."
var string tt44="TP1 and TP2 as R multiples. TP1 % of the position is taken at TP1 and the stop moves to break-even for the rest."
var string tt45="Trades still open after this many bars are closed at the bar close. One Trade at a Time: no new signal while a trade is open."
var string tt46="Draw entry/SL/TP lines for each trade and keep at most this many past trades on the chart. Stats always include every trade."
var string tt47="Dashboard with market context, open position and per-grade results: trades, win rate (any positive result), average R, profit factor. Results assume entry at the signal bar close and exclude commissions/slippage."
var string tt48="Session VWAP line. Also used as confluence: longs above VWAP and shorts below VWAP get +1 point."
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~}

